<title>FRANCE: U.S. Secretary of State Albright arrives in Paris.</title>
<headline>U.S. Secretary of State Albright arrives in Paris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Secretary of State Madeleine Albright, on her maiden foreign trip since taking office, arrived in France on Monday for talks on NATO enlargement and reform of the Atlantic Alliance.</p>
<p>Arriving from Bonn, Albright was met at Paris's Orly Airport by French protocol officials and was due to have talks with President Jacques Chirac, Prime Minister Alain Juppe and Foreign Minister Herve de Charette later on Monday before flying on to London on Tuesday.</p>
</text>
